  <h2>Prepare delivery and product listing</h2>
  <p>Before accepting a proposal, explain your address, receiving hours and delivery constraints. A city centre shop and a logistics platform have different access and storage facilities. Check the proposed packaging and the information needed for your operation. On arrival, compare the goods with the delivery documents, retain traceability information and report discrepancies to your contact. Planning these steps from the first purchase makes repeat ordering easier.</p>
  <p>For sales in France or another EU country, review the food information for the destination market. The <a href="https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/labelling-and-nutrition/food-information-consumers-legislation_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">European Commission explains consumer food information rules</a>, including allergens and labelling. An official entertainment licence does not replace these checks. Ask your supplier for the relevant information and confirm the requirements that apply to your activity.</p>
  <h2>Build a manageable first selection</h2>
  <p>First define the purpose of the offer: extending a drinks section, creating a manga corner or testing impulse references. Choose complementary categories rather than several products serving exactly the same use. Our <a href="{{ path('app_products.en') }}">ULTRAPOP product ranges for professionals</a> page distinguishes drinks, savoury snacks, confectionery and instant noodles. Identify universes relevant to your customers and then request confirmation of availability for your country.</p>
  <p>After launch, record sales by reference, stockouts and remaining stock. A missing product tells you something different from a product that is displayed but rarely purchased. Keep a simple record to decide what to reorder and which new products to test. Our <a href="{{ path('app_article_merchandising.en') }}">licensed product merchandising guide</a> explains how to organise displays without changing the entire section for every test.</p>
  <h2>What a clear first enquiry looks like</h2>
  <p>You could describe your project as follows: “We are a specialist grocery store in France. We would like to explore manga drinks and savoury snacks for a dedicated corner. Could you confirm available references, packaging, order terms and delivery costs for our address?” Include estimated volumes if you know them; you do not need to invent a quantity before understanding the sales units.</p>
  <p>At LNS Trade, a <a href="{{ path('app_wholesale.en') }}">wholesale drinks and snacks pricing request</a> starts this conversation. Minimum quantities, prices and transport arrangements depend on the selection and destination. The form does not place an order or commit you to a purchase. For requirements beyond licensed ranges, our <a href="{{ path('app_trading.en') }}">food sourcing, import and distribution service</a> can also assess your project.</p>
